  "extraction_notes": [
    "Datasheet hash verified as a9a81555b7497aedd932f1d50115c245a8331ce51ca98c1306aa16a4af4202be.",
    "Figures 1 and 2 are static characteristics at TJ = 25 degC unless otherwise indicated, using pulses shorter than 300 us and maximum 0.5% duty cycle per note E; only the 25 degC transfer curve was digitized because Figure 2 also contains a 125 degC curve.",
    "Figure 1 includes additional VGS = 5 V, 6 V, and 10 V curves, but their high-current portions exceed or approach the 120 A plot limit; the four fully readable lower-gate-drive curves are extracted.",
    "Figure 8 capacitance traces were digitized as plotted over VDS = 0 to 30 V. The table gives VGS = 0 V, VDS = 15 V, f = 1 MHz; the electrical-characteristics heading specifies TJ = 25 degC unless otherwise noted.",
    "The table's corresponding maximum values are RDS(ON) = 7.5 mOhm at VGS = 10 V, ID = 20 A, TJ = 25 degC; 11.3 mOhm at VGS = 10 V, ID = 20 A, TJ = 125 degC; 10.5 mOhm at VGS = 4.5 V, ID = 20 A, TJ = 25 degC; Ciss = 1380 pF, Coss = 235 pF, Crss = 150 pF, and VSD = 1 V. The schema has no separate maximum fields for these quantities, so their meanings are retained here.",
    "The table also publishes minimum capacitances Ciss = 920 pF, Coss = 125 pF, and Crss = 60 pF; minimum/typical/maximum gate-charge values, trr, and Qrr are not represented by dedicated schema fields and are omitted from specs rather than mapped to an unrelated field.",
    "The body-diode characteristic is plotted in Figure 6, but the schema's curve structure is used for transfer, output, and capacitance families only; the tabulated typical VSD is retained in specs."
  ],
